Ariana Grande is an American singer, songwriter, and actress. She first gained fame in 2010 when she was cast in the Broadway musical &quot;13.&quot; She later starred in the Nickelodeon television series &quot;Victorious&quot; and &quot;Sam &amp; Cat.&quot; 

Grande&#39;s music career began in 2011 when she released her debut single &quot;Put Your Hearts Up.&quot; However, it was her second album, &quot;My Everything,&quot; that launched her into superstardom. The album, which was released in 2014, included hit singles such as &quot;Problem&quot; and &quot;Break Free.&quot; 

Grande&#39;s subsequent albums, including &quot;Dangerous Woman&quot; and &quot;Sweetener,&quot; were also commercial successes. She has won numerous awards throughout her career, including a Grammy Award, multiple Billboard Music Awards, and multiple MTV Video Music Awards. 

In addition to her music career, Grande has been involved in philanthropic work. She has donated money to various charitable organizations and has been involved in causes such as fighting for gun control and raising awareness for mental health. 

Grande has also been recognized for her fashion sense and has been featured in various fashion magazines. She has collaborated with various fashion designers, including Givenchy and Reebok. 

Overall, Ariana Grande is one of the most successful and influential pop stars of the 21st century. Her powerful vocals, catchy hooks, and relatable lyrics have made her a favorite among music fans around the world. Her music continues to be popular today, and she remains a role model for young women around the world.
